    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "A door that implements the AdvInteractable trait.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 3/9: TRAIT IMPLEMENTER (Door)\nA trait is a contract (types/traits/AdvInteractable.trait.json): `interact(instigator_id)` and\n`set_highlight(enabled)`. A Blueprint opts in under Class Settings > Traits, which writes the trait's id\ninto this class (blueprint_metadata.implemented_trait_ids). It then MUST provide each trait method:\na custom event with the same name and parameters. The compiler refuses the class until it does.\nCallers (a player, an interaction trace) can then talk to ANY implementer without knowing its class.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -290
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          190
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. BEGIN PLAY - nothing trait specific happens here; the contract is satisfied by the two\ncustom events below.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          -80
        ],
        "size": [
          680,
          270
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "bp_log"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. TRAIT METHOD interact(instigator_id) - implemented as a custom event with the SAME name and\nparameter. A locked door refuses; otherwise it counts the use, flips `is_on` (Not) and logs the new state.\nWhoever called the trait method (a player, an AI) is `instigator_id`; here we only count uses.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          160
        ],
        "size": [
          2700,
          710
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "it",
          "it_used",
          "it_inc",
          "it_set_used",
          "it_on",
          "it_not",
          "it_toggle",
          "it_if",
          "it_log_on",
          "it_log_off",
          "it_locked",
          "it_lock_if",
          "it_locked_log"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. TRAIT METHOD set_highlight(enabled) - the interaction system calls it when the player looks at or\naway from the object. A real object would drive an outline or emissive material here; the\nexample just stores the flag so a debugger can show it.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          1530
        ],
        "size": [
